    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0281" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">792.94/14</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Siamese Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Prince Damras</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-18">May 18, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hornbeck</hi>: You have no doubt seen
                    articles in the newspapers of the 13th and 14th May that Siam’s neighbours are
                    alarmed by the increasing influence of Japan, and that some sort of special
                    treaty has been signed with that country.</p>
                <p>Remembering that you have once asked me about the Japanese influence in my
                    country, and I then said that I had no information respecting <pb facs="0282"
                        n="170" xml:id="pg170"/> the matter, I am now in a position to inform you
                    that there is no truth in the reports given by the Associated Press to the
                    various newspapers, and I am instructed to assure you that it is the policy of
                    His Majesty’s Government to strengthen the bonds of friendship with all the
                    treaty Powers alike, and not with any single one in particular.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Damras</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
